## Phase 2.3 VERIFIED (2026-09-25, qemu -vga none -display none)
- Root-caused original fork #PF: process_fork/create_user/destroy, elf_load, mmap all
  restored to paging_get_directory() = &physical_directory[0] (KERNEL dir) on syscall
  exit, so the ring-3 resume ran under kernel CR3 where 0x40000000+ is unmapped
  (fault CR3 0x29e000 = kernel_pml4 phys; PML4[0]=0x29f023, PDPT[1]=0 matched).
- Fix: paging_get_active() (returns active_dir) used at every switch-restore point:
  process.c fork/create_user(201)/destroy(G 261-262), elf.c (93,224), mmap.c (44,81,106).
  Scheduler compare + idle/kernel dir anchors unchanged.
- "Parent never resumed" was an instrumentation artifact: screen_scroll did full
  framebuffer clear (fb_fill, 1024x768 pixel walk) on every wrap; with -vga std
  -display none each wrap cost ~1.4s via FIFO-stalled string of writes, so debug
  spam timed runs out. No exception under qemu -d int,cpu_reset. Fixed: screen_scroll
  -> fbcon_scroll (memmove rows + clear last row only).
- Removed schedule/kprintf probe spam; isr.c per-IRQ serial prints removed.
- Found+fixed libc bug: wait() cast &status to (int), sign-extending the pointer to
  0xffffffffbfffefdc (kernel USER_ADDR_MAX 0xFFFF800000000000 rejected it) -> status
  never written back. Fixed cast to (long).
- Boot/perf: headless QA uses -vga none (VGA text path, fb_detect fails -> fast);
  -vga std + -display none LFB writes are the pathological slowness (QEMU artifact).
- RESULT (3/3 runs, 15s timeout): child "my fork() returned 0" + exit 7; parent
  "wait() reaped PID 4 with status 7"; "wait(-1) with no children -> -1 (errno 10)";
  hello exits 0; "myos>" shell prompt reached. No Unhandled/fault dumps. Phase 2.3 PASS.

## Phase 2.4 VERIFIED (2026-09-25, qemu -vga none -display none)
NX + SMEP + user-stack guard page.

Changes:
- EFER.NXE (NX) + CR4.SMEP, both CPUID-gated (CPUID leaf 0x80000001 EDX[20]
  for NX, leaf 7 EBX[7] for SMEP); unsupported CPUs skip the bit instead of
  #GP'ing on the CR4/EFER write. Gate print: "[CPU] NX=1 SMEP=1".
- NX (bit 63) honored in paging_map, paging_get_physical (masked in both
  4KB and 2MB-huge paths so NX never leaks into a returned physical
  address — the Phase 2.4 #GP root cause), paging_get_attrs (leaf NX kept).
- NX on writable ELF segments (both elf loaders) + all user-stack pages.
- Stack guard page: lowest user-stack page left unmapped; overflow #PF's
  with CR2 in the guard range instead of scribbling over ELF mappings.
- Process fork's eager-copy preserves exact per-page attrs (NX/exec/W) via
  paging_get_attrs so exec pages stay executable in the child.

QA:
3/3 headless boots (qemu -vga none):
- [CPU] NX=1 SMEP=1 on every boot; no Unhandled/Panics.
- forkdemo 3/3: child exits 7, parent reaps PID with status 7, wait(-1)->-1
  (errno 10), shell prompt "myos>" reached.
- Guard-page #14 verified via a TEMPORARY user/stacktrip.elf spawn:
  CR2=0xBFFFBF98 (stack-bottom/guard), leaf PT unmapped in walk, clean halt,
  no memory corruption. The TEMP spawn was reverted; forkdemo regression
  re-verified 3/3 after the revert.
